simple: add radial lens shading correction to the soft IPA and GPU debayer

Add an Lsc algorithm to the soft IPA, configured from the tuning file
(optional optical centre as a fraction of the width and height, and
k1, k2, k3 per colour channel), and apply the radial gain
1 + k1 r^2 + k2 r^4 + k3 r^6, clamped to [1, 4], in the GPU debayer
shaders after black level subtraction and before the white balance
gains and the colour matrix. The IPA reports whether the correction is
enabled at init time so that the GPU debayer only compiles it in when
configured; the CPU debayer logs a warning and ignores it.

